["div",{"c":"scene","i":"sc11-card"},["div",{"c":"scene-head"},["h3",{"i":"sc11"},"Scene 11 · Act 4: prove the impact on completed returns"],["div",{"c":"chips"},["span",{"c":"chip"},"45:00–50:00"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"Act 4 · Prove"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"RFP 4.15, 4.49–4.55"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"Sam"]]],["div",{"c":"scene-body"},["p",{"c":"goal"},["strong",0,"Goal:"]," Move from clicks to completed returns and revenue, measured in their warehouse, with the analyst answering follow-up questions himself."],["div",{"c":"prep"},["h4",0,"Prep before the scene"],["ul",0,["li",0,["span",{"c":"tab"},"A14"]," Optimizely Analytics: saved exploration on the synthetic warehouse dataset from 9.6 (experiment decisions, “return completed” events, revenue per client). Filters reset."],["li",0,"Section 10 does not build this dataset. If it isn't ready, use the fallback below."],["li",0,"Decide the one filter you will change live (for example new vs. returning clients)."]]],["table",{"c":"beats"},["thead",0,["tr",0,["th",0,"Beat"],["th",0,"What to say"],["th",0,"What to show"]]],["tbody",0,["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-tell"},"Tell"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“Optimizely Analytics runs on your warehouse, your Snowflake or Databricks, so there's no copy of client data, and the test is measured against outcomes your finance team already trusts. This is 4.15 and 4.49 to 4.55.”"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"tab"},"A14"]," the exploration."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-show"},"Show"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“Here's UrgencyB's lift on completed returns and revenue per visitor, not just clicks. The dataset is synthetic for the demo.”"]],["td",0,"Point at the lift on “return completed” and revenue per visitor."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-show"},"Show"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“And Sam can answer the follow-up question himself, in the meeting, without a ticket to the data team.”"]],["td",0,"Change the filter you chose live (for example new vs. returning) and read the result."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-back"},"Tell back"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“From clicks to completed returns: 4.15 and 4.49 to 4.55. And because experiments are causal, these results are clean inputs your mix-modeling team can use to calibrate their model.”"]],["td",0,"Clock: ",["span",{"c":"clock"},"Next Tue 10:30"]," impact confirmed."]]]],["div",{"c":"fallback"},["strong",0,"If it breaks:"]," If the exploration isn't ready, stay on the Feature Experimentation results (",["span",{"c":"tab"},"A13"],") and describe warehouse-native analysis in one sentence: “In Optimizely Analytics this same result is measured against your warehouse data.” Don't improvise numbers."],["p",{"c":"transition"},["strong",0,"Transition:"]," “One last piece. On Friday morning leadership wants to know what we learned this week.”"]]],
["div",{"c":"scene","i":"sc12-card"},["div",{"c":"scene-head"},["h3",{"i":"sc12"},"Scene 12 · Close: the weekly decision digest and the recap"],["div",{"c":"chips"},["span",{"c":"chip"},"50:00–53:00"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"Close"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"RFP 5.17, 5.19, 4.22"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"Sam, leadership"]]],["div",{"c":"scene-body"},["p",{"c":"goal"},["strong",0,"Goal:"]," ",["span",{"c":"moment"},"Moment 3"]," Show the leadership readout produced by an agent, then tell back the whole story and the three things, in the same words as the Opening."],["div",{"c":"prep"},["h4",0,"Prep before the scene"],["ul",0,["li",0,["span",{"c":"tab"},"A3"]," Mark with ",["span",{"c":"clip"},"C9"]," ready. The pre-generated report is open in ",["span",{"c":"tab"},"A15"]," (the agent takes minutes, so start it and switch)."],["li",0,["span",{"c":"tab"},"A1"]," slide 4: the recap timeline from Tuesday 9:02 to the Friday digest."]]],["table",{"c":"beats"},["thead",0,["tr",0,["th",0,"Beat"],["th",0,"What to say"],["th",0,"What to show"]]],["tbody",0,["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-tell"},"Tell"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“Your RFP describes sixteen in-season decision cycles, and every week someone has to turn results into a readout for leadership. This is 5.17 on operating cost.”"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"tab"},"A3"]," Mark."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-show"},"Show"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“The Program Overview agent pulls the week together: test velocity, win rate, the biggest winners and what we learned, compared with last week, ready to email to leadership.”"]],["td",0,"Paste ",["span",{"c":"clip"},"C9"]," and send. Switch straight to the saved report in ",["span",{"c":"tab"},"A15"],": “here's this morning's run.” Scroll velocity, win rate, top winners, learnings."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-tell"},"Tell"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“Let's replay Maya's week. Request at 9:02. Brief by 9:06. Legal approved by 9:15. A local page built by 9:30. Office data current, and a personalized page live by 9:40. A test launched in under five minutes. A week later, the winner live for everyone in seconds, and on Friday the digest.”"]],["td",0,"Switch to ",["span",{"c":"tab"},"A1"]," slide 4. Point along the timeline as you speak."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-back"},"Tell back"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“So, the three things. The winning version went live in seconds, with no dev ticket. A marketer launched a test on her own in minutes. And it plugged into what you already have. In your leadership's words, expert-led and technology-enabled. This is the technology getting out of the experts' way.”"]],["td",0,"Slide 4, the three lines."]]]],["div",{"c":"fallback"},["strong",0,"If it breaks:"]," If Mark is slow or the agent handle fails, just use the saved report. Don't wait for the live run."],["p",{"c":"transition"},["strong",0,"Transition:"]," “Let me show how this fits next to what you've already built, and how we handle taxpayer data.”"]]],
["div",{"c":"scene","i":"sc13-card"},["div",{"c":"scene-head"},["h3",{"i":"sc13"},"Scene 13 · Architecture, trust and the next step"],["div",{"c":"chips"},["span",{"c":"chip"},"53:00–60:00"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"Architecture, trust, Q&A"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"RFP 5.12–5.14, 8.x"],["span",{"c":"chip"},"Presenter, AE"]]],["div",{"c":"scene-body"},["p",{"c":"goal"},["strong",0,"Goal:"]," Show coexistence with their Adobe, Salesforce and warehouse investments, state only confirmed trust facts, handle questions, and ask for a scoped proof of concept."],["div",{"c":"prep"},["h4",0,"Prep before the scene"],["ul",0,["li",0,["span",{"c":"tab"},"A1"]," slide 5 (coexistence architecture), slide 6 (trust), slide 7 (next step)."],["li",0,"Slide 6 contains only confirmed statements: documented U.S. hosting for ODP (US region), Optimizely Analytics (AWS US-East-1) and Mark (US region). Everything else on residency and IRC 7216 is shown as “confirming in writing” until Section 8 items are closed."],["li",0,"Q&A prep (11.5) on your second screen."]]],["table",{"c":"beats"},["thead",0,["tr",0,["th",0,"Beat"],["th",0,"What to say"],["th",0,"What to show"]]],["tbody",0,["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-tell"},"Tell"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“You've invested in AEP, Journey Optimizer, Salesforce Marketing Cloud and your warehouse. We're not asking you to rip any of that out. This is 5.13 and 5.14.”"]],["td",0,"Slide 5."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-show"},"Show"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“Content lives in the CMS and is delivered through Graph to the web, the app and, by API, your messaging tools. Decisions happen on the server in Feature Experimentation. Real-time audiences come from ODP. Analytics reads your Snowflake or Databricks. Creative and approvals run in CMP and the DAM.”"]],["td",0,"Walk the slide-5 flows left to right."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-show"},"Show"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“On taxpayer trust: personalization is designed to be consent-aware, which IRC 7216 requires. For data residency, ODP, Optimizely Analytics and Mark are documented with U.S. hosting, and we'll confirm the rest, including backups and logs, in writing in our response.”"]],["td",0,"Slide 6. Do not go beyond what is on the slide."]],["tr",0,["td",{"c":"beat"},["span",{"c":"b-tell"},"Tell"]],["td",0,["span",{"c":"say"},"“Our suggestion for a next step is a scoped proof of concept: one late-season landing page, one CMS-driven experiment and one CMP workflow, measured against the clock you described earlier, the time from decision to live. Who should we work with to set that up?”"]],["td",0,"Slide 7. Then open the floor for questions."]]]],["p",{"c":"transition"},["strong",0,"Transition:"]," ",["span",{"c":"stage"},"(End. Thank them, confirm follow-ups and owners, and stop sharing.)"]]]],
["h3",{"i":"s-qa"},"11.5 Q&A prep: likely questions and short answers"],
["table",0,["thead",0,["tr",0,["th",0,"Likely question"],["th",0,"Short answer"],["th",0,"Where to point"]]],["tbody",0,["tr",0,["td",0,"Can you deliver weekly MMM?"],["td",0,"No native MMM. Experiments give causal lift that your MMM team can use to calibrate the model (9.5). Don't demo it."],["td",0,"Scene 11"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Do we have to replace AEP or Journey Optimizer?"],["td",0,"No. Optimizely runs alongside them: content through Graph, decisions in Feature Experimentation, audiences from ODP or synced from your CDP."],["td",0,"Slide 5"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"How do you stop two tests or a test and a personalization colliding?"],["td",0,"Exclusion groups between tests, and one server-side decision point that checks personalization first, then the test."],["td",0,"Scenes 8–9"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"What can marketers do without developers?"],["td",0,"Build pages from governed blocks, create variations, set up and ship tests. Developers build new block types and integrations."],["td",0,"Scenes 6, 9, 10"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Where is our data stored? U.S. only?"],["td",0,"ODP, Optimizely Analytics and Mark have documented U.S. hosting. We'll confirm the other products, including backups and logs, in writing."],["td",0,"Slide 6; Section 8"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"How do you handle IRC 7216?"],["td",0,"Personalization is designed to be consent-aware; our contractual position will come from Legal in writing. Don't improvise."],["td",0,"Slide 6; Section 8"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"How fast does ODP qualify a visitor?"],["td",0,"Usually within seconds; under 90 seconds in 99.999% of cases per the docs. Not for 100%-instant use cases."],["td",0,"Scene 8"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Does personalization slow the page or cause flicker?"],["td",0,"Decisions run on the server before render, using a cached project file, so there is no flicker."],["td",0,"Scene 8"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Can winners publish automatically?"],["td",0,"The docs say Mark can choose the winning content variation automatically. ",["span",{"c":"verify"},"Verify"]," it in your instance before saying so."],["td",0,"Scene 10"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"How long does implementation take?"],["td",0,"Don't quote a timeline. Propose the scoped PoC and size the rest from it. (This demo took one SA about six days; that is not a production estimate.)"],["td",0,"Slide 7"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Is this real H&R Block data?"],["td",0,"No. All content, offices, audiences and results are synthetic."],["td",0,"Opening"]]]],
["h3",{"i":"s-recovery"},"11.6 Recovery playbook"],
["table",0,["thead",0,["tr",0,["th",0,"If this happens"],["th",0,"Do this"],["th",0,"Say this"]]],["tbody",0,["tr",0,["td",0,"Persona doesn't switch (Scene 8)"],["td",0,"After about 30 seconds, show the variation in the CMS Editor preview. Use the override only if it was deployed."],["td",0,"“While ODP catches up, here's exactly what Dana sees.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Office card doesn't update (Scene 7)"],["td",0,"Move on; check again after Scene 8; show the Graph query as proof."],["td",0,"“Propagation takes a moment; I'll come back to it.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Mark is slow or gives an odd answer"],["td",0,"Open the saved output in ",["span",{"c":"tab"},"A15"],"."],["td",0,"“Here's the one I ran this morning with the same prompt.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Flag change not on the Live App (Scene 10)"],["td",0,"Wait up to 45 seconds; open a fresh private window; then the CMS backup or the recorded clip."],["td",0,"“The site checks for changes about every thirty seconds.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Blueprint or publish fails (Scene 6)"],["td",0,"Switch to “Phoenix (backup)”."],["td",0,"“Let me use the copy I prepared earlier so we stay on time.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Analytics exploration not ready (Scene 11)"],["td",0,"Stay on the Feature Experimentation results."],["td",0,"“In Optimizely Analytics the same result is measured against your warehouse.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"SSO, network or Live App down"],["td",0,"Switch to the recorded walkthrough in ",["span",{"c":"tab"},"A15"]," and narrate it live."],["td",0,"“I'll walk you through the recording so we keep to time.”"]],["tr",0,["td",0,"Running behind"],["td",0,"Shorten Scene 5 to one asset; skip the optional Robert beat in Scene 8; keep Scenes 9, 10 and 12 intact."],["td",0,"(Nothing; just keep the three moments.)"]]]],
["h3",{"i":"s-after"},"11.7 After the demo"],
["ol",{"c":"steps"},["li",0,"Reset per 10.16: copy ",["code",0,"OriginalBackup"]," to Original and publish; restore the A/B rule on ",["code",0,"hrb_landing_hero_test"]," in Production (shipping concluded it), or switch to a duplicate “ready” flag; run ",["code",0,"yarn seed:offices --open 0"],"; open ",["code",0,"/api/demo/persona?p=reset"],"."],["li",0,"Delete or unpublish the Phoenix page; delete the live CMP request; delete the Development A/B rule created in Scene 9."],["li",0,"Within 24 hours, send the follow-up: thank-you, the recording (if allowed), the PoC proposal, answers to open questions, and the Section 8 items still being confirmed."],["li",0,"Write down what landed and what didn't for the next run, especially their Scene 1 answer and any questions you couldn't answer."]]
